  "sharedCorrection": {
    "storage": "Existing SvgCpuClipCoverage owns lazily allocated, single-channel output bitmaps for retained affine/binary viewport contours. Samples use the owning canvas bitmap independently of native construction bounds and per-bitmap border coverage.",
    "readers": "SvgRasterClipMask exposes identical canvas-coordinate reads for RGBA tapes, compact owners and analytic rectangles. Binary regions, opacity/mask restoration and narrow construction clips use those shared reads.",
    "rounding": "The existing contour mapper, analytic/fallback rasterizer and binary line-edge construction produce unchanged alpha. Parent output and native borders intersect independently with the original byte multiplication.",
    "reservation": "The original full-RGBA clip payload reservation remains live and admits the compact payload: a pixel occurs in at most four overlapping native bitmaps. Per-bitmap descriptors and array headers are separately reserved before allocation. No pool/cache, growth peak or remaining-budget decision is introduced.",
    "lifetime": "Clip frames own the original capacity reservation and coverage metadata through all synchronous borrowers. Isolated layers explicitly suspend output masks while retaining construction metadata. Denial/cancellation cleanup and retry remain asserted.",
    "scope": "Retained affine viewport, binary viewport and exclusion contours use compact output. General vector masks, enclosing clip resources and RGBA compositing keep their existing owners and paths; no symbol-specific shortcut or new supported feature."
  },
